<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh names first woman ambassador.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh names first woman ambassador.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh appointed its first woman ambassador on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Mahmuda Haque Chowdhury was named ambassador to Bhutan, the the official BSS news agency said.</p>
<p>It said Chowdhury was also the first Bangladeshi woman to join the foreign service, in 1972. She is currently serving as deputy chief of protocol in the foreign ministry.</p>
